2026-07-15 12:15:48,972 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-07-15 12:15:48,973 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To ensure compliance with the tender's requirements, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can implement several security controls and measures. Firstly, regarding GDPR compliance, our standard data residency is EU-only, which aligns with the requirement of hosting data exclusively within the European Union. We also have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside the EU unless there is an explicit legal basis, ensuring no unauthorized data transfer.

For data protection, we utilize anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models to pseudonymise sensitive data where applicable. Additionally, our Data Protection Officer (DPO) is appointed and can be contacted at dpo@nexus-engineering.it for any GDPR-related inquiries or concerns.

To address explicability and transparency, we have the capability to conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs), which helps in understanding and mitigating risks associated with personal data processing. Our average DPIA duration is 3 weeks, ensuring timely assessment and compliance.

For security, our access control standards include multi-factor authentication (MFA) enforced through TOTP or hardware tokens (FIDO2), role-based access control (RBAC) design experience, and privileged access management (PAM) solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault. Sessions timeout after 30 minutes of inactivity, and we support SSO protocols such as SAML 2.0 and OpenID Connect.

Our network security architecture patterns include Zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth. We have IDS/IPS deployed and experience with DDoS mitigation. Annual penetration testing plus post-major release testing is conducted with partners like Synacktiv (France) and HN Security (Italy), ensuring our systems are secure.

Regarding AI security controls, we protect against prompt injection, perform output PII redaction, detect adversarial inputs, and have a confidence threshold escalation mechanism in place. Model isolation is ensured through an inference API without direct model access for end-users, and we conduct security reviews for model updates.

To ensure the solution is designed as a tool of assistance with no automated decisions without explicit validation by an agent, our AI systems are designed to provide intelligent assistance tools that facilitate decision-making without automating decisions. This aligns with our experience in regulatory frameworks such as GDPR and the EU AI Act, ensuring that our solutions support agents in their tasks without replacing human judgment.

By implementing these measures, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can ensure compliance with the tender's requirements regarding GDPR, explicability, transparency, security, and the design of the solution as a tool of assistance.
